CORE
main.c
--program-only
^\(\d+\) dynamic_object#\d+\.\.key == 1$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^\(\d+\) dynamic_object#\d+\.\.values\[\[\d\]\] == dynamic_object#\d+\.\.values
^\(\d+\) dynamic_object#\d+\.\.key == dynamic_object#\d+\.\.key$
--
At the join after the allocation, which fails on the other branch, the
object's fields were not assigned on that branch (generation zero): the merged
value of each field is its value on the allocating branch, which symbolic
execution used to copy into a new generation, one assignment per field of the
object.  Symbolic execution now continues with the allocating branch's name.
